    the recommendation, for the requester, follows the auditor decision
      ✔ is withheld from the requester until an auditor has decided
      ✔ is always visible to the auditors and reviewers
      ✔ is shown to the requester once the auditor has allowed the request
      ✔ never shows the requester the digest of the auditor note
      ✔ is shown to the requester once the auditor has decided, in every part of the trail
      ✔ is withheld from a court reviewer for their own request until another auditor has decided
      ✔ is withheld from an audit district head for their own request until another auditor has decided
      ✔ keeps an audit district head out of the auditor view of their own request
      ✔ stays withheld from the requester when the request ends without a decision

